    "final_answer": "I have gathered all the information needed. Here's the complete summary:\n\n## 🍣 Homemade Sushi Recipe (Allrecipes)\n\n**Source:** https://www.allrecipes.com/spicy-homemade-sushi-recipe-20154/\n**Author:** 1ORANGE1\n**Rating:** 4.5 out of 5 stars — **217 Ratings, 147 Reviews** ✅ (well above the minimum 20)\n**Total Time:** 1 hr 5 mins (Prep: 40 mins, Cook: 25 mins) | **Yield:** 4 cut rolls (8 servings)\n\n### 📊 Nutrition Facts (per serving)\n| Nutrient | Amount |\n|---|---|\n| Calories | 152 kcal |\n| Fat | 4 g (Saturated: 1 g) |\n| Carbohydrates | 26 g (Fiber: 2 g, Sugar: 7 g) |\n| Protein | 4 g |\n| Sodium | 703 mg |\n| Cholesterol | 6 mg |\n\n### 🥢 Main Ingredients\n1. 1 ⅓ cups water\n2. ⅔ cup uncooked short-grain white rice\n3. 3 tablespoons rice vinegar\n4. 3 tablespoons white sugar\n5. 1 ½ teaspoons salt\n6. 4 sheets nori seaweed\n7. ½ pound imitation crabmeat (flaked)\n8. 1 avocado (peeled, pitted, sliced)\n9. ½ cucumber (peeled, cut into small strips)\n10. 2 tablespoons pickled ginger\n\n### 🗄️ How to Store These Rolls\nThe official recipe page does not include a dedicated \"How to Store\" section. The directions end with slicing and do not specify storage. However, the Allrecipes community Q&A on this page provides the only storage guidance available:\n\n> **Community answer from user \"tcasa\":** *\"You can make sushi in advance, however, depending on what you use for the filling (tuna, salmon, etc) it will not last more than a day in the fridge.\"*\n\n️ Note: This storage tip is a community-contributed response, not the recipe author's official instruction. For best food safety with rice and seafood fillings, refrigeration within 1 day is generally recommended; for longer keeping, freezing is not recommended because the rice texture and nori degrade.",
